[ti:Week05-Mon.mp3]

[00:00.00]decline 熟义 n. （数量、价值、质量等的）减少，下降，衰落‖v. 减少，衰退；谢绝 示例 ① Over the past two years, the figures on imports and exports seem not to signal a double-dip recession—a renewed decline in the broad level of economic activity in the United States— but an economic expansion. 在过去两年里，进出口数据似乎并未显出二次衰退的迹象——美国经济活动的大范围新一轮衰退， 相反却表明美国经济在扩张。（2011. 12）② There has been a decline in the value of the U.S. dollar and a corresponding increase in the strength of the euro. 美元的价值有所下跌，而欧元的实力则相应有所上升。
[00:12.67]explode 熟义 v. 爆炸；迸发（感情） 示例 ① It is time to do for enterprise what such ageing rockers have done for pop music: explode the myth that it is a monopoly of the young. 现在是时候把这些高龄摇滚乐手对流行音乐所做的贡献——打破“流行音乐是年轻人专利”的神话——应用到商业领域了。（The Economist） ② According to observers, a powerful time bomb exploded shortly after the plane took off. 据目击者说，飞机起飞后不久一枚威力巨大的定时炸弹就爆炸了。
[00:22.22]absurd 熟义 a. 荒谬的，荒唐的；怪诞不经的 示例 ① He also predicts that "absurdly wasteful" displays of wealth will become unfashionable while the importance of close-knit communities and families will become clearer. 他还预言说以“荒谬的挥霍”来炫耀财富将过时，而社区和家庭紧密结合的重要性将更加明显。（2008. 6）② His story of being kidnapped by aliens was so absurd that it was laughable. 他声称自己被外星人绑架的故事荒唐得令人发笑。
[00:31.87]series 熟义 n. 一系列，一连串；系列节目 示例 ① A series of tests in recent years has shown, Mr. Carr points out, that after spending time in quiet rural settings, subjects "exhibit greater attentiveness, stronger memory and generally improved cognition. Their brains become both calmer and sharper." 卡尔先生指出，在最近几年里经一系列测试证明，在安静的田园环境中待一段时间后，被测试者“表现得注意力更集中，记忆力更强，而且认知能力普通提高。这些人的大脑会变得更冷静和敏锐。”（2012. 12）② The whereabouts of that sum of money sparked off a whole series of problems that nobody had foreseen. 那笔钱的下落引发一连串谁都没有料到的问题。 语料 Life is just a series of trying to make up your mind. 生活只是由一系列下决心的努力所构成。（英国军事理论家富勒）
[00:48.10]roar 熟义 v. 咆哮；叫喊；呼啸而行‖n. 咆哮，吼叫（声） 示例 ① In his early days as an investment celebrity he would appear as a pundit on television shows and roar at his fellow panellists for being too cynical. 在他初为投资名人的时候，他常以投资权威人士的身份出现在电视节目里，并冲着同组成员咆哮，指责他们太愤世嫉俗。（The Economist） ② The comedian's hilarious imitation of the politician was greeted with a roar of laughter. 该喜剧演员对政治家的滑稽模仿引起了哄堂大笑。
[00:58.22]facility 熟义 n. 设施；天资，才能 示例 ① While college facilities sit idle, they continue to generate maintenance expenses that contribute to the high cost of running a college. 尽管大学设施闲置， 但他们还是会不断产生维护费，这导致高校运营成本居高不下。（2012. 6）② Students are encouraged to avail themselves of the full range of the university's facilities. 学校鼓励学生充分利用大学的各种设施。
[01:07.14]historical 熟义 a. (有关)历史的；历史学的；历史题材的 示例 ① Historically, humans get serious about avoiding disasters only after one has just struck them. 历史上，人类只有在遭受了灾难打击之后才会对避免灾难严肃对待。（2007. 6）② This hall has an amazingly wide collection of pens and paper of different historical periods from different countries. 这个馆汇集了各个历史时期来自各个国家的纸和笔。
[01:15.93]electronic 熟义 a. 电子的；电子设备的‖[pl.] n. 电子学；电子工业 示例 ① In a division of electronics engineers, who are designing equipment so advanced that they work in teams of up to 150. 在电子工程师分组，由于该组成员都是设计先进设备的，所以他们组的智商高达150。（2013. 6）② The electronic dictionary consists of thousands of electronic parts. 这个电子词典由成千上万个电子元件构成的。
[01:24.35]integrity 熟义 n. 诚信，正直；完整，完好 示例 ① The former ethic suggested success was founded on integrity, modesty, loyalty, courage, patience, and so forth. 前一种道德准则暗示成功建立在正直、谦虚、忠诚、勇气和耐心等品质的基础上。（2011. 12）② Our company will maintain the attitude of integrity, quality, and excellent service to cooperate with you. 我们公司将秉承诚信的态度、优质的质量和优良的服务与各位合作。
[01:33.49]apparatus 熟义 n. 仪器；（尤指政党或政府的）机构， 组织 示例 ① For decades researchers have probed the brain with all manner of sophisticated apparatus. 数十年来，研究人员已经利用各种精密仪器对大脑进行探测。（The Economist）② I nearly suffocated when I entered the burning building without breathing apparatus. 当我未佩戴呼吸器进入那座燃烧着的大楼时，我差一点窒息了。
[01:41.50]personality 熟义 n. 性格；气质 示例 ① The personality ethic suggested it was one's attitude, not behaviour, that inspired success, and this ethic was founded on a belief of positive mental attitude. 性格魅力暗示成功取决于个人态度而非行为，且这种魅力建立在对积极心态的信念之上。（2011. 12）② Your handwriting is often a reflection of your personality. 一个人的笔迹往往反映出这个人的个性。
[01:50.23]incentive 熟义 n. 激励，刺激，鼓励；诱因 示例 ① A small gasoline tax would help free America from its dependence on oil imports and create incentives for green energy development. 小额的汽油税将有助于美国摆脱对石油进口的依赖，并促进绿色能源的发展。（2012. 6） ② As long as there is demand for wildlife products, the financial incentive for poachers will be there. 只要对野生动物制品有需求，偷猎者行动的经济诱因就会存在。
[01:59.49]ritual 熟义 n. 程序，礼节；老规矩，惯例‖a. 仪式上的，庆典的；老套的，惯常的 示例 ① Every year, after Americans have stuffed themselves on Thanksgiving feasts, a significant portion of the population chooses to participate in the ritual sport known as Black Friday, where shoppers are elbowed, shoved, and trampled in the name of getting good deals. 每年吃完感恩节大餐后，许多美国人便会参加名为“黑色星期五”的习惯性消遣， 众多购物者以买便宜货为名你推我挤，互相踩踏。（The Economist） ② She went through her usual ritual of making sure all the doors and windows were locked before she left for work. 出门上班前，她按照惯例检查了家里所有的门窗是否都已锁上。
[02:14.06]subscribe 熟义 v. 订阅，订购；同意，赞成 示例 ① Its practice of "bundling" journals forces libraries which wish to subscribe to a particular publication to buy it as part of a set that includes several others they may not want. 它将刊物捆绑出售的做法， 迫使只想订阅特定刊物的图书馆不得不将包含他们可能不想要的刊物的一整套全部买下。（The Economist） ② The authorities no longer subscribe to the view that disabled children are unsuitable for ordinary schools. 当局不再支持残疾儿童不适合进入普通学校的观点。
[02:25.31]emerge 熟义 v. (从隐蔽处)浮现；（事实、意见等） 暴露 示例 ① In many countries immigrants have been filling such gaps in the labour force as have already emerged (and remember that the real shortage is still around ten years off). 在许多国家，移民一直在填补已经出现的劳动力短缺（但请记住，真正的短缺大约将出现在十年后）。（2010. 12） ② The company emerged from the court case with its reputation intact. 这家公司挺过了这场官司，名誉丝毫未受到损害。
[02:34.99]image 熟义 n. 形象；画像 示例 ① Humans, says Edward M. Hallowell, have the ability to call up images of bad things that happened in the past and to anticipate future events. 爱德华•M.哈洛韦尔说，人类拥有回忆起过去发生的不好事情的情景和预测未来事件的能力。（2006. 12）② Advertisements aim at improving the image of the product. 广告旨在提升产品形象。
[02:42.74]duplicate 熟义 v. 复制，复印；（尤指不必要时）重复 a. 完全一样的；复制的， 副本的‖n. 完全一样的东西；复制品，副本 示例 ① It also has too many layers of government: provincial, regional and local administrations that often duplicate rather than replace the activities of central government. 政府层级繁多：省、 区、地级政府的管理经常重复而不是代替中央政府发挥作用。（The Economist） ② All the employees have received duplicated notices of the meeting. 所有的雇员都收到了同样的会议通知。
[02:53.27]favourite 熟义 a. 特别受喜爱的‖n. 特别喜爱的人（或事物）；受宠的人 示例 ① Your least-favourite reporter suggests a dumb story idea. 你最不喜欢的记者提出了一个愚蠢的报道创意。（2011. 6）② The President stressed a favourite campaign theme—a sounder social welfare system. 总统强调了最受人欢迎的竞选主题——更加健全的社会福利体系。
[03:00.26]analysis 熟义 n. 分析；分析的结果 示例 ① Wikipedia credits the technique to Albert Humphrey, an academic at Stanford University, who based it on an analysis of Fortune 500 companies that he carried out in the 1960s and 1970s. 维基百科把这一方法归功于斯坦福大学的一名学者艾伯特•汉弗莱。他在二十世纪六七十年代基于这一方法分析了《财富》杂志评出的世界500强公司。（The Economist）② Analysis showed that traces of toxic substances were present in the cup. 分析显示杯子中有微量有毒物质。
[03:10.86]frequency 熟义 n. 发生率，频率；频繁 示例 ① Within the next 20 years, space planes could be taking off for the Moon at the same frequency as airplanes flying between New York and Los Angeles. 在未来20年之内，航空飞机将能够像在纽约和洛杉矶之间穿梭的飞机一样频繁地飞往月球。（2006. 12） ② This device can help us have a better understanding on the frequency, intensity and duration of storms. 这个设备能帮助我们更好地了解暴风雨的发生频率、强度和持续时间。
[03:20.78]fatal 熟义 a. 致命的；灾难性的 示例 ① According to the Aviation Safety Network, an independent database in the Netherlands, there were 23 fatal airliner accidents during 2012, with some 475 people killed as a result. 根据荷兰独立数据库航空安全网络的统计，2012年共发生了23 起灾难性的飞机事故，共475人在事故中遇难。（The Economist）② All medicines have side effects, some of which can be fatal. 所有药物都有副作用，有些副作用甚至可能是致命的。
[03:30.62]refrain 熟义 v. 克制，节制；避免 示例 ① You hear the refrain all the time: the U.S. economy looks good statistically, but it doesn't feel good. Why doesn't ever-greater wealth promote ever-greater happiness? 你一直听人们重复说：美国经济从数据上看很好，但人们感觉并不好。为什么财富的不断增加没有促进幸福程度的不断提高呢？（2007. 6）② He has refrained himself from arguing with the peddler. 他克制住自己没有和那个小商贩吵起来。
[03:39.92]compute 熟义 v. 计算；估算 示例 ① There must be a problem with the computing system. 肯定是计算系统出现了问题。（2008. 6）② A failure to compute correctly may result in the explosion of aircraft. 计算失误可能会导致飞机爆炸。
[03:44.87]satisfactory 熟义 a. 令人满意的，够好的 示例 ① She has got a satisfactory job in another company. 她已经在另外一家公司找到了满意的工作。（2008. 6）② Satisfactory completion of university course can by no means ensure you a job. 圆满完成大学课程绝不能确保你能找到工作。
[03:50.67]multitude 熟义 n. 众多，大量；群众 示例 ① The explosive growth of Internet services such as e-mail, music downloads, video streaming, Internet television and, above all, the web itself, with its multitude of applications, has overwhelmed the digital world's capacity to reflect upon what has passed before. 互联网服务爆炸性的增长，比如电子邮件、 音乐下载、视频观看、国际电话，尤其是网络本身的众多应用，远远超过了数字世界反映以前发生事件的能力范围。（The Economist） ② It is the government's duty to feed the starving multitude. 使饥饿的群众有饭吃是政府的职责。
[04:03.31]hospitality 熟义 n. 好客，殷勤；（款待客人等的）食物 示例 ① As the latest rover arrives on Mars to assess its hospitality, astronomers are learning more about possibly habitable worlds beyond the solar system. 随着用来评估宜居性的最新的探测器抵达火星，天文学家正在了解更多太阳系以外可能宜居的星球。（The Economist）② Let me hope that I may receive you in my country some day and reciprocate the truly warm welcome and generous hospitality extended to me. 希望将来有一天我可以在我国接待你，并回报你给予我的热烈欢迎和盛情款待。
[04:14.90]counsel 熟义 n. （尤指年长者或专家的）劝告，建议；辩护律师‖v. 提供专业咨询；建议，劝告 示例 ① Another aspect of social comparison in the counselling context relates to a tecДique known as normalising. 在咨询时，社会比较的另外一个方面与一种被称作“正常化”的技巧相关。（2012. 12）② The center provides free counselling service to those victims whose relatives were killed in the earthquake. 该中心为在地震中失去亲人的受害者提供免费的咨询服务。
[04:24.46]supreme 熟义 a. （级别或地位）至高无上的；（程度）很大的，最大的 示例 ① In Britain, unlike America, the Supreme Court cannot strike down statutes as unconstitutional because Parliament itself is supreme. 与美国不同， 英国的最高法院无权裁定议会立法不符合宪法，因为议会本身是至高无上的。（The Economist） ② He is the supreme exponent of the English realistic literature. 他是英国现实主义文学的重要代表。
[04:33.19]cheerful 熟义 a. 快乐的，兴高采烈的；令人愉快的 示例 ① It urges seamen to be cheerful in all circumstances. 它（英国皇家海军）鼓励船员在任何情况下都要保持快乐的心态。（The Economist） ② She seems amazingly cheerful considering all she's had to go through since her husband died. 自从丈夫去世后，她经历了种种磨难，但她看起来还是那么快乐，真是令人惊讶。
[04:40.50]ingenious 熟义 a. 精巧的，精妙的；心灵手巧的；机敏的 示例 ① All this interest implies that sending people to Mars is merely a matter of political will and a bit of ingenious engineering. 所有这些兴趣表明，将人类送上火星不过是政治意愿加一点巧妙的工程设计而已。（The Economist） ② It took a lot of imagination to come up with such an ingenious way of saving energy. 设计出如此精妙的节约能源的方法需要有极大的想象力。
[04:49.39]rival 熟义 n. 竞争对手‖v. 与…相匹敌，比得上 示例 ① After all, more than 200 years separated Einstein from his nearest rival, Isaac Newton. 毕竟，爱因斯坦和能够与他匹敌的艾萨克•牛顿之间隔了200多年。（2010. 12） ② He gained an upper hand over his rivals in the competition to get control of the company. 他在争取公司控制权的竞争中占了上风。
[04:56.76]steer 熟义 v. 驾驶（船、汽车等）；行驶 示例 ① Many find it difficult to steer away from a career path or make a change, even if it doesn't feel right. 许多人发现即使感觉不对劲也很难转换其职业道路或是做出改变。（2007. 6）② She managed to steer the conversation away from the unpleasant topic. 她设法把谈话从这个不愉快的话题上转移开。
[05:03.86]commit 熟义 v. 做出（错或非法的事），犯；承诺 示例 ① For example, the shortage of young adults is likely to make countries more reluctant to commit the few they have to military service. 例如，因为青少年短缺，使一些国家不愿让他们仅有的为数不多的年轻人服兵役。（2010. 12） ② Police arrested the rioters for committing a breach of the peace. 警察以妨碍治安罪逮捕了暴乱者。
[05:11.89]combat 熟义 n. 搏斗，打仗，战斗‖v. 防止，减轻； 与…搏斗 示例 ① The government argues that the expressway is needed to combat congestion on nearby roads, where the volume of traffic is forecast to grow by 20% by 2020. 政府说需要修建高速公路来应对周边道路的拥堵问题，预计该区域的交通流量在2020年前会增加20%。（The Economist） ② The government proposed the new legislation designed to combat racism in the work place. 政府颁布了旨在抵制工作场所种族歧视的新法规。
[05:22.01]uranium 熟义 n. 铀（放射性化学元素） 示例 ① Uranium is usually extracted from ore that contains 1,000 or more parts per million (ppm) of the element. 铀通常是从含铀量在百万分之一千以上的铀矿中提取出来的。（The Economist） ② Niger is the world's largest exporter of uranium. 尼日尔是世界上最大的铀输出国。
[05:28.66]swell 熟义 v. 肿胀；（使）凸出；（使）增大‖n. 海浪的涌动；（尤指身体部位）鼓出处，隆起处 示例 ① According to a recent report from UN-HABITAT, the United Nations agency for human settlements, the population of some cities is set to swell by up to 85% in the next 15 years. 根据联合国人居署近期的一个报告，有些城市的人口在接下来的15 年里可能会增加高达85%。（The Economist） ② Do not be swollen by victory. 别被胜利冲昏了头脑。
[05:37.68]radical 熟义 a. 根本的；激进的，极端的‖n. 激进分子 示例 ① He pledged radical measures to snap Japan out of its long economic funk and restore pride to a country nearly overwhelmed by a sense of decline. 他采取激进措施使日本摆脱长期的经济萧条并使这个几乎被经济衰退之势击垮的国家重塑信心。（The Economist） ② She experienced a radical change. 她发生了根本的变化。
[05:45.46]subordinate 熟义 n. 下级‖a. 隶属的，从属的，下级的；次要的‖v. （把…）置于次要地位，（使…）从属于 示例 ① The musically adept are better able to concentrate on a biology lesson despite the noise in the classroom or, a few years later, to finish a call with a client when a colleague in the next office starts screaming at a subordinate. 擅长音乐的人更能够在并不安静的生物课上集中注意力；这些人在数年之后更能够在隔壁办公室同事大声训斥下属的情况下与客户完成电话沟通。（2012. 6）② Personal interests should subordinate to those of the collective. 个人利益应该服从集体利益。
[05:57.79]crane 熟义 n. 起重机，吊车；鹤‖v. 伸长（脖子） 看；探头看 示例 ① Rubbish that cannot be recycled is lifted by a crane onto barges for incineration. 不可回收的垃圾被吊车装上驳船运去焚烧。（The Economist）② The audience at the back craned their necks to get a better view of the stage. 后排的观众伸长了脖子想把舞台看得更清楚一些。
[06:04.78]conspicuous 熟义 a. 易见的，明显的；显著的；惹人注意的；出类拔萃的 示例 ① Some of the new rich are splashing out on Porsches and big houses, but most prefer to spend their money in subtler and less conspicuous ways. 一些新富花大价钱购置保时捷和豪宅，但他们中的大多数花钱低调，不那么招摇。（The Economist）② Recent years have seen conspicuous development in space tecДology. 近几年航空科技有了显著发展。
